Mr. President, Brazil welcomes the delegation of Belarus. Brazil commands the continued efforts of Belarus to combat trafficking in persons, as well as its cooperation with regional and international partners in this regard. We encourage the country to strengthen legal and institutional protections for children and families, particularly to support victims of violence, including sexual violence, with focus on vulnerable families. In a constructive spirit, Brazil recommends that Belarus, one, declare a moratorium on the application of the death penalty and consider acceding to the second optional Protocol to the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights; 2. revise domestic legislation regulating public assemblies, associations and the media, including anti-terrorism laws, with a view to ensuring its compatibility with international human rights standards and safeguarding civic space;

Thank you.

We wish Belarus a constructive and successful review.
